course: dictionary
lesson: 9584
title: Streaky: lines, stripes and luck
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Streaky means having streaks, which are long thin lines or marks of a different colour. The lines are often uneven, not neat and straight. «A tawny owl sleeps by day in streaky brown feathers that match bark» tells you the owl's feathers have lines of colour on them.
explain: Context helps here. The owl sleeps by day, and its feathers match bark, so the feathers must look like the rough wood of a tree. Streaky brown feathers have light and dark lines in them, so the owl blends in and stays hidden.
explain: Streaky has two other meanings you may meet. Streaky bacon has stripes of fat and meat. In sport, a streaky shot is not steady, and it may be a lucky edge. Ask yourself: is the word talking about lines, food or sport? The words around it will tell you.
fact: Streaky means having streaks: long thin lines or marks of a different colour.
fact: Streaks are often uneven, so «streaky windows» and «streaky hair dye» look patchy.
fact: «Streaky bacon», in the UK, Ireland and Australia, has stripes of fat and meat, cut from the belly.
fact: In sport, «streaky» means not steady: sometimes very good, sometimes bad. In cricket, a «streaky shot» is a lucky edge.
fact: The comparison forms are streakier and streakiest.
exercise: «A tawny owl sleeps by day in streaky brown feathers that match bark.» What does streaky describe? | Its food, which is small birds | *Its feathers, which have lines of colour | Its voice, which is loud | Its nest, which is high up
exercise: «Streaky bacon» is sold at the shop. What kind of food is it? | *Bacon with stripes of fat and meat | Cold, raw bacon in a tin | Bacon with no fat at all | Bread with seeds on top
exercise: Sam says, «That was a streaky shot.» What does streaky mean in cricket? | A shot that hits the stumps every time | *A lucky edge, not a steady shot | A shot that is quiet and slow | A very long, high hit
test: «The windows were streaky after Dad cleaned them.» What does streaky mean here? | Cracked into pieces | Shiny and perfectly clean | *Having marks or lines left on the glass | Frozen solid
test: Which meaning fits «a streaky shot» in cricket? | Stripes of fat and meat | Long thin lines of colour | Very quiet | *A lucky edge, not steady
exam: «A tawny owl sleeps by day in streaky brown feathers that match bark; if small birds or crows find it, they mob it with loud alarm calls.» What do the small birds and crows do? | They sing a lullaby to the owl | They build a nest around the owl | *They mob the owl with loud alarm calls | They bring the owl a meal of bacon
